==================================================

Use typed props.

Example:

---
interface Props {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
}

const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

Use interfaces or appropriate types.

Avoid unnecessary `any`.

Components should have clear contracts.

Example:

---
interface Props {
  image: string;
  alt: string;
  priority?: boolean;
}
---

==================================================

==================================================

For static generation:

---
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await getPosts();

  return posts.map((post) => ({
    params: {
      slug: post.slug
    },
    props: {
      post
    }
  }));
}

const { post } = Astro.props;
---

Use props rather than unnecessarily refetching the same data.

For runtime/server rendering, dynamic routes can be resolved on request when the project is configured appropriately.

==================================================

==================================================

Use API endpoints when you need an actual HTTP endpoint.

Examples:

src/pages/api/users.ts
src/pages/api/products/[id].ts
src/pages/feed.xml.ts

Endpoints can expose:

GET
POST
PUT
PATCH
DELETE

Return proper Response objects.

Example:

export async function GET() {
  return new Response(
    JSON.stringify({ success: true }),
    {
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json'
      }
    }
  );
}

Validate input.

Authenticate protected endpoints.

Never expose secrets.

==================================================
